invariant: INV-35
file: build.h
catches: test/lib-pair-check.sh
reason: build.h gives the QUIC transport's build record the tcp-nonblocking
  transport's name, so two transports name their build records alike again, as every
  object did before docs/decisions.md 61. A QUIC object then defines
  ch_build_info_tcp_nonblocking while PUBLIC names ch_build_info_quic_nonblocking: nmedit refuses to
  package it on macOS, and objcopy localizes it elsewhere, so the QUIC
  half of cocuyo's pair links against the tcp-nonblocking object's build record
  and ch_build_matches answers 0. test/lib-pair-check.sh objects either
  way.

--- old
#define ch_build ch_build_info_quic_nonblocking
--- new
#define ch_build ch_build_info_tcp_nonblocking
